  "inline_use": "the key is read and used on one line, so there is no name to follow -- those rows are counted but cannot be sole authority by construction",
  "population": "E340's self_bound rows only: the producer loads the key off its own published face into a name (results/state_tilt/ALLOWANCE-2026-11-01.json -> 18 rows)",
  "sole_authority": "nothing downstream compares the name and nothing downstream tests it: the value the producer last wrote is the only authority for whatever it feeds.  Aliases are followed (``p = permit.strip()`` counts as the permit) up to four hops, and every row publishes ``alias_names`` so a reader can see how far the study looked",
  "write": "``face[key] = value`` is a store into the loaded dict, not a grant: those are counted in ``accesses_excluded_as_writes`` and the entries whose only access was a store are listed in ``write_only_entries``.  E340's line-shaped classifier counted them as bound reads, which is why its 18 is larger than the number of real reads here"
 },
